+# Experiment G3 — knob sweep toward Goal X: faster cycle-safe retract
+
+You are `codex` (gpt-5.6-terra, medium). Work ONLY in this worktree
+(`/Users/chrishafley/projects/sprefa-wt-g3-knob-sweep`), crate `v6/sprefa-store`
+(own `[workspace]` — `cd v6/sprefa-store` first).
+
+## Goal X
+
+Make `cascade::retract_dred` faster WITHOUT changing its result. This is a
+RESEARCH sweep: try ~10 knobs one at a time, measure each against a fixed
+baseline, and report which move the needle. You are producing a findings table,
+not a merge — but DO leave any clearly-winning knob applied + committed.
+
+## The profile you are optimizing against (already measured)
+
+At 960k nodes the retract is 100% CPU, ZERO disk I/O (fully page-cached +
+temp_store=MEMORY), ZERO network. Access paths are already optimal (index seeks).
+The only non-seek cost the plans show is `USE TEMP B-TREE FOR DISTINCT` on the 3
+hot frontier-expansion joins. So the knobs most likely to help are ones that cut
+per-round materialization or bytecode work, NOT I/O knobs (measure them anyway to
+CONFIRM they do nothing).
+
+Read `src/cascade.rs` (the statements), `examples/profile_dred.rs` (how to
+measure I/O + rounds), and `examples/explain_plans.rs` (how to read plans).
+
+## Baseline + measurement protocol (do this FIRST, pin the numbers)
+
+Baseline = current `retract_dred` at 960k and 2.9M:
+```
+cd v6/sprefa-store
+cargo build --release --example profile_dred
+DL_MEMCAP_MB=2048 ./target/release/examples/profile_dred 6 160000 0   # 960k
+DL_MEMCAP_MB=2048 ./target/release/examples/profile_dred 6 480000 0   # 2.9M
+```
+Record `retract wall` ms (run each 3x, report min/median — do NOT trust one run).
+For EVERY knob you must ALSO prove the survivor set is byte-identical: use the
+hermetic hash harness — the out_hash must not change:
+```
+cargo build --release --example perf_report
+DL_MEMCAP_MB=2048 ./target/release/examples/perf_report sqlite-dred-loop 6 160000 0
+# baseline out_hash at 960k = dd6a707234617ea5 ; at 2.9M = 454c5271a7e5a260
+```
+A knob that changes out_hash is REJECTED, no matter how fast. Gun stays pointed
+(DL_MEMCAP_MB set) on every run.
+
+## The knobs to sweep (do each in isolation, revert before the next)
+
+Measure delta-ms at 960k for each; keep the ones that help, note the ones that do
+nothing (that is a finding too — e.g. I/O knobs should be flat since I/O is zero):
+
+1. **DISTINCT → INSERT OR IGNORE**: drop `SELECT DISTINCT` on the 3 frontier
+   joins and rely on the `cx_next` / `cx_frontier` PRIMARY KEY to dedup via
+   `INSERT OR IGNORE`. Kills the `USE TEMP B-TREE FOR DISTINCT`. (Most promising.)
+2. **`key IN (SELECT ...)` → `UPDATE ... FROM`**: rewrite the 4 kill/mark UPDATEs
+   as `UPDATE cx_row SET weight=0 FROM cx_frontier WHERE cx_row.key=cx_frontier.key`
+   (SQLite 3.33+). Compare plans + ms.
+3. **cache_size**: sweep `PRAGMA cache_size` = -65536 / -262144 / -1048576
+   (64MB/256MB/1GB). (Expect ~flat past db-fits-in-cache; confirm.)
+4. **mmap_size**: sweep 0 / 268435456 / 1073741824 / 4294967296.
+5. **page_size**: 4096 vs 8192 vs 16384 (must be set BEFORE schema create).
+6. **journal_mode** for the retract: WAL vs MEMORY vs OFF (retract makes no
+   durable rows we need to survive a crash mid-op — safe to test OFF here).
+7. **synchronous**: OFF vs NORMAL during the retract.
+8. **threads**: `PRAGMA threads=4` (helps the sort/temp-b-tree steps, if any).
+9. **WITHOUT ROWID on the working tables** (cx_frontier/cx_next/cx_cone are single
+   INTEGER PK already = rowid tables; try WITHOUT ROWID and compare).
+10. **Frontier ping-pong**: instead of `DELETE cx_frontier; INSERT ... FROM cx_next`
+    each round, alternate two tables so you drop 2 statements/round. (Structural.)
+
+Bonus if time: combine the top-2 winners and measure the stack.
+
+## Constraints
+
+- Never change the RESULT of `retract_dred` (out_hash gate above).
+- Do not touch `retract` (counting) or `retract_dred_cte`.
+- No new dependencies. No CTEs (measured slower already).
+- The full `cargo test --release` must stay green after any knob you KEEP.
+
+## Style laws
+
+Descriptive names; no em dashes; no `eprintln!`; N+1 forbidden; no
+`provenance`/`substrate`/`load-bearing`/`regime` identifiers.
+
+## Communicate back
+
+Write `v6/sprefa-store/EXPERIMENT-G3-KNOBS-RESULT.md`: a ranked table with columns
+`knob | 960k ms (min/median, 3 runs) | 2.9M ms | out_hash unchanged? | verdict`,
+the baseline row on top, one line per knob, and a final "what to keep" section.
+Commit any winning knob you applied (with the full test suite green) on this
+branch. Do not touch other crates or the main checkout.
